Sigma rules bundled in lib/sigma/sigmahq-rules.json
===================================================

The detection rules in lib/sigma/sigmahq-rules.json are taken from the SigmaHQ
rule repository (https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma), release pinned in
scripts/sigma-update.ts (see "release" / "commit" in the JSON). They are
imported by `npm run sigma:update` from rules/windows/** with their title, id,
author, references, description, tags, false positives and SigmaHQ path left
intact. The only transformation is YAML → JSON (and dropping rules the engine
cannot run on EVTX, listed in lib/sigma/sigmahq-skipped.json).

Each rule's author(s) are identified in its "author" field; the original rule
is at https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/<release>/<path>. The viewer shows
"Rule by <author>, SigmaHQ, DRL 1.1" and the rule link with every match, and
CSV/JSON exports carry the same attribution and link on every row.

